+            Callable[[Exception], None] | None,
+            Doc(
+                """
+                An optional callback to be invoked when a registered startup
+                event handler raises an exception.
+
+                When set, exceptions raised by startup handlers are passed to
+                this callback and are **not** propagated, allowing the
+                application to continue starting up. When not set (the
+                default), exceptions raised by startup handlers propagate
+                normally, preserving the existing behavior.
+
+                This is useful to gracefully handle recoverable startup
+                failures (e.g. a database connection that is briefly
+                unavailable) without crashing the whole application.
+                """
